   "basis": "The Environmental Permitting (England and Wales) Regulations 2016, Schedule 23 Part 3, Table 2 'Concentration of radionuclides', concentration in becquerels per gram (Bq/g), for a solid or relevant liquid. Part 3 states that this Table 2 is the one referred to in paragraph 5 of Part 2 (processed radionuclides of natural terrestrial or cosmic origin) and paragraph 6 of that Part (radionuclides not of natural terrestrial or cosmic origin); the regulation does not call it a clearance table. Its summation rule: the sum of A/B, A the concentration of each listed radionuclide and B its column 2 value. Bq/g converted to Bq/kg (x1000). The suffix '+' (or 'sec') means the parent is in secular equilibrium with the daughters in Table 3 and its value is for the parent alone but already takes the daughters into account; covered_by_parent lists the Table 3 daughters. Where a parent is printed in several forms the form with the smallest limit is kept and progeny coverage follows that form (see the sidecar).",
